type: software
title: "The simulator decides the verdict: a pre-registered audit of evaluation shortcuts for AI trading agents in electricity balancing markets"
authors:
  - alias: gepapak
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-29"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - multi-agent reinforcement learning
  - electricity markets
  - imbalance settlement
  - backtesting
  - evaluation methodology
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  Controlled, internally pre-registered audit of how simulator shortcuts (no liquidity cap, no solvency,
  zero-floor cash accounting, percent-of-price payoffs, interpolated prices) change the verdict on AI trading
  agents in the Danish imbalance-settlement market. Includes the engine source, an audit patch, aggregated
  results of 264 engine evaluations, a ledger-reconciliation tool, an evaluation checklist and a code-level
  prevalence audit of 21 public electricity-RL environments.
